WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.105
Module two:

2
00:00:01.105 --> 00:00:02.547
wallets and security.

3
00:00:02.547 --> 00:00:06.529
Where coins really live, what a key and a seed phrase are,

4
00:00:06.529 --> 00:00:08.794
and how money is most often lost:

5
00:00:08.794 --> 00:00:12.158
not to a network hack, but to your own signature.

6
00:00:13.158 --> 00:00:14.950
A wallet does not hold coins:

7
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.607
they are always recorded in the blockchain.

8
00:00:17.607 --> 00:00:19.399
A wallet holds a private key,

9
00:00:19.399 --> 00:00:22.859
a secret number that gives the right to sign a transfer.

10
00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:27.245
If the exchange holds the keys, you only have a record in its database.

11
00:00:27.245 --> 00:00:30.644
If only you hold the key, nobody can freeze your coins,

12
00:00:30.644 --> 00:00:33.486
but nobody can help you recover access either.

13
00:00:34.486 --> 00:00:36.554
Both options have their own risk.

14
00:00:36.554 --> 00:00:41.002
In November 2022 the FTX exchange halted withdrawals and went bankrupt:

15
00:00:41.002 --> 00:00:43.571
the company itself had used client money.

16
00:00:43.571 --> 00:00:48.896
And thousands of people have lost their seed phrase or sent coins to the wrong place,

17
00:00:48.896 --> 00:00:50.713
with no way to get them back.

18
00:00:50.713 --> 00:00:54.598
So the question is not whether it is safe, but whom you trust.
